        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Whisky Poker',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Whisky Poker is a poker-style game with widow hand exchange. Multiple players. 5 each + 5-card widow. Options: swap entire hand for widow (old hand becomes new widow face-up), swap 1 card with widow, or knock (triggers final round). Last best poker hand after knock wins. Worst hand pays chip.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Whisky Poker is an American commerce game based on poker hand rankings but with a different mechanism: improving hands by exchanging with a common table hand (the widow). It appears in many late 19th- and early 20th-century North American card game books and is less well known today. A version remains popular in Mexico as La Viuda (the widow).',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card pack without jokers; one deck for all player counts (2 to 9).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards, chips',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '5 each + 5-card widow face-down.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
